      "id": 71732,
      "name": "Envisioner",
      "username": "Envisioner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-11-15T05:02:02.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So, does this mean that you always fully resolve cards first before acknowledging triggers, even if they're triggers on the card being played, such as Negative Energy Field and Surprise Shopping Trip?&nbsp; I was always under the impression these would happen \"as\" the card was played, before it entirely \"hit the table\" and moved on to the resolving of its effects.&nbsp; Or am I comparing apples to oranges here, because playing cards functions differently than using powers?&nbsp; Can a newly-played villain target (say one of Gloomweaver's relics) be one of the targets which NEF damages?&nbsp; Can a 1-HP Legacy play Fortitude during an SST without instantly dying?</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:50:59.263Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
