      "topic_slug": "timing-confusion-with-toxic-seaweed",
      "display_username": "Envisioner",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>So, does this mean that you always fully resolve cards first before acknowledging triggers, even if they&#39;re triggers on the card being played, such as Negative Energy Field and Surprise Shopping Trip?&nbsp; I was always under the impression these would happen &quot;as&quot; the card was played, before it entirely &quot;hit the table&quot; and moved on to the resolving of its effects.&nbsp; Or am I comparing apples to oranges here, because playing cards functions differently than using powers?&nbsp; Can a newly-played villain target (say one of Gloomweaver&#39;s relics) be one of the targets which NEF damages?&nbsp; Can a 1-HP Legacy play Fortitude during an SST without instantly dying?</p>",
